message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "A certified approximation of the Chen-LeBrun-Weber Einstein metric"
authors:
  - name: "Moki & Julio"
date-released: 2026-11-13
version: "1.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24188065"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hashirama1337s/certified-chen-lebrun-weber"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - Chen-LeBrun-Weber metric
  - Einstein metric
  - extremal Kähler metric
  - Abreu equation
  - computer-assisted proof
  - interval arithmetic
  - Newton-Kantorovich
  - Laplace eigenvalues
abstract: >-
  A computer-assisted, interval-arithmetic location of the Chen-LeBrun-Weber Einstein metric on CP2#2(-CP2): an explicit
  degree-84 polynomial potential with a certified H^6 radius of 7.568e-10 for the conformally related extremal Kähler metric
  and a pointwise bound d_h <= 5.504e-8 for the Einstein metric, conditional on cited inputs (one a preprint). Corollary: exactly
  one scalar Laplace eigenvalue in (0, 2 Lambda). Every sealed test, including 16 FAILED, is listed. Data and code included.
